# Hello Harry - the full document round-trip, driven like a human would:
#
#   1. open a real text editor
#   2. type "hello harry" with real keystrokes
#   3. save through the editor's own Save dialog (Ctrl+S, name, Enter)
#   4. close the editor
#   5. open the saved file again from disk and read it back to prove it
#      persisted
#
# Run it:   hawk.exe --file examples\hello-harry.hawk
# Dry run:  hawk.exe --dry-run --file examples\hello-harry.hawk
#
# Result:   %USERPROFILE%\Documents\hello-harry.txt containing "hello harry",
#           reopened on screen, with a screenshot in shots\reopened.png.
# Hold ESC or Ctrl+Alt+H to abort at any point.

del ~\Documents\hello-harry.txt
open notepad
wait 2400
focus Notepad

type hello harry
key ctrl+s
wait 2000

type hello-harry.txt
key enter
wait 2000

close Notepad
waitclose Notepad 8000
wait 1500

open ~\Documents\hello-harry.txt
wait 2600
focus Notepad
read ~\Documents\hello-harry.txt
shot hello-harry-opened.png
windows 6

log hello harry: created, written, saved and reopened
